# sing-box proxy credentials.
#
# Copy to ~/.config/sing-box/secrets.env (mode 600) and fill in the six values.
# install.sh does that copy for you on a fresh machine.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE TEMPLATE AND IS COMMITTED. The filled-in copy lives outside
# the repo and must never enter git. After changing any value: proxyctl reload
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fastest way to fill this in
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The 3x-ui panel can hand you every value at once. Open the panel →
# Inbounds → your VLESS inbound → the client's QR code or "copy link" button.
# You get a URL shaped like this, and every field below is in it:
#
#   vless://VLESS_UUID@VLESS_SERVER:VLESS_PORT
#         ?type=tcp&security=reality
#         &pbk=VLESS_PBK&sni=VLESS_SNI&sid=VLESS_SID
#         &fp=chrome&flow=xtls-rprx-vision#label
#
# If you would rather read them off the panel's own fields, each variable below
# says where. 3x-ui renames things between versions, so treat the labels as a
# strong hint rather than an exact string match — the client link is canonical.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The address clients connect to: your server's public IP, or the domain
# pointing at it. This is the host part of the client link (between "@" and
# ":"). The panel's own inbound "Address" field is sometimes blank or a
# placeholder when it is set to auto-detect, so prefer the link.
VLESS_SERVER=

# The inbound's listening port — the number after ":" in the client link, and
# the "Port" column on the Inbounds list.
VLESS_PORT=

# The client's UUID. Expand your inbound in the Inbounds list to see its
# Clients table; this is the "ID" column. Each client has its own UUID — use
# the one belonging to this machine, not another device's.
VLESS_UUID=

# The SNI presented during the TLS handshake — "sni=" in the client link.
# In the panel it is the Reality "SNI" field, and it must be one of the
# hostnames listed in the inbound's "Dest" / "Target". A mismatch fails the
# handshake with an unhelpful error.
VLESS_SNI=

# The PUBLIC half of the Reality keypair — "pbk=" in the client link, and the
# "Public Key" field in the inbound's Reality settings.
#
# The panel shows the private key next to it. Do not put that here: the private
# key belongs only on the server, and a client never needs it.
VLESS_PBK=

# The Reality short ID — "sid=" in the client link. The panel generates a list
# of them under "Short IDs"; any entry works, but use the one from the link you
# copied so client and server agree.
VLESS_SID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not configured here
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# flow (xtls-rprx-vision) and the uTLS fingerprint (chrome) are hardcoded in
# proxy/config.template.json, because they describe how this client behaves
# rather than which server it talks to. If your inbound uses a different flow,
# edit the template — not this file.
